          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hsk1_9_g_ne",
      "number": 4,
      "title": {
        "hanzi": "用“呢”问在哪儿",
        "english": "Using 呢 to ask where something is"
      },
      "explanation": {
        "hanzi": "名词 + 呢？ 如果前面没有别的话，常常是问这个人或东西在哪儿。",
        "english": "When noun + 呢？ is said on its own, without an earlier sentence to compare with, it usually means \"Where is ...?\" — for example when you are looking for something. 我的猫呢？ = Where's my cat? (After a statement, as in Lesson 4, noun + 呢 means \"What about ...?\")"
      },
      "examples": [
        {
          "hanzi": "我的猫呢？",
          "pinyin": "Wǒ de māo ne?",
          "english": "Where's my cat?"
        },
        {
          "hanzi": "安娜呢？",
          "pinyin": "Ānnà ne?",
          "english": "Where's Anna?"
        },
        {
          "hanzi": "我的杯子呢？",
          "pinyin": "Wǒ de bēizi ne?",
          "english": "Where's my cup?"
        },
        {
          "hanzi": "爸爸呢？——他在医院。",
          "pinyin": "Bàba ne? —— Tā zài yīyuàn.",
          "english": "Where's Dad? — He's at the hospital."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
